# Line endings.
#
# This repo is edited from Windows (C:\Users\Dave\repos) and from Linux hosts
# (khpi5, zorin). Without a rule here, Git stored whatever each machine wrote,
# so the same file flipped between CRLF and LF and showed as "modified" with a
# whole-file diff containing no actual change. On 2026-07-25 that was 18 files
# and 2,940 changed lines, all of it noise — and noise that hides real edits.
#
# text=auto: Git decides text vs binary by content.
# eol=lf:    text files are normalised to LF in the repo AND in the working
#            tree. LF (not native) is deliberate — shell scripts and Dockerfiles
#            in here are executed on Linux, where a CRLF shebang fails.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these.
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.epub filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.onnx binary
*.pt binary
*.bin binary
